// `continue` to the condition skips the step clause and either loops forever
// or produces a wrong count, silently. tests/c/030_control.c covers it.
//
// A missing condition (`for (;;)`) leaves the cond block with an
// unconditional edge to the body, so only a `break` leaves the loop.

